&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Présentation du poste :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Au sein de l’équipe technique d’Artefact, vous rejoignez une communauté de Software Engineers en tant que Manager et référent technique auprès de nos grands comptes clients. Dans un environnement à forte accélération sur la Data et l’IA Générative, vous intervenez pour piloter des projets d&#39;ingénierie complexes, encadrer les équipes et porter l&#39;excellence opérationnelle et technique.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ce qu’on attend de vous :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;En tant que Manager, vous supervisez la conception et le déploiement d&#39;architectures critiques (Data Platforms, Agentic Platforms) tout en assurant l&#39;encadrement, le mentorat et le développement de carrières des membres de l&#39;équipe. Vous jouez un rôle clé dans la relation client, le cadrage technique des affaires et le rayonnement de la communauté tech Artefact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vos missions :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Piloter et encadrer la réalisation de projets Data &amp;amp; IA complexes (ex. solutions multi-agents LangGraph sur Kubernetes, architectures Médaillon).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superviser le cadrage et la construction de Data Platforms robustes sur GCP, AWS, Azure ou Snowflake en garantissant l&#39;alignement avec les meilleures pratiques d&#39;Infrastructure as Code (IaC) et d&#39;ingénierie logicielle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Définir la vision technique des projets GenAI / LLM (orchestration, évaluation, contrôle) et promouvoir l&#39;usage quotidien des coding agents au sein des équipes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assurer la gestion de carrière, le suivi de performance et le mentoring continu des Software Engineers sous votre responsabilité.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mener les cadrages techniques auprès des clients grands comptes et défendre avec pédagogie les choix stratégiques et d&#39;architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Veiller au respect des standards de qualité de code, de sécurité et de livrables sur l&#39;ensemble de vos périmètres applicatifs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribuer activement à l&#39;animation de la communauté technique (Talks Tech, Guildes, REX) et participer au processus de recrutement et de montée en compétences de la pratique.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profil recherché :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expérience &amp;amp; Leadership :&lt;/strong&gt; Expérience confirmée en tant que Lead / Engineering Manager ou Senior Architect ayant déjà encadré des équipes techniques et piloté des projets stratégiques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Résolution de problèmes :&lt;/strong&gt; Solides intuitions techniques et capacité à traduire des enjeux business complexes en architectures techniques pérennes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Management &amp;amp; Transmission :&lt;/strong&gt; Posture bienveillante, pédagogique et exemplaire, à l&#39;aise pour faire grandir les talents, donner du feedback constructif et animer une équipe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Spécialisations (au moins 1) :&lt;/strong&gt; Expertise avérée en Analytics Engineering, Software Development, SRE, Cloud Architecture ou AI Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stack technique :&lt;/strong&gt; Maîtrise avancée de l&#39;écosystème tech (Python, FastAPI, dbt, LangGraph, Docker, Terraform, GCP, AWS, Azure, Snowflake, Kubernetes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process de recrutement :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HR Interview (30-45 min) :&lt;/strong&gt; Échange sur votre parcours, vos compétences managériales et l&#39;adéquation culturelle avec un Talent Acquisition Specialist.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Deep Dive (60 min) :&lt;/strong&gt; Session de live coding et d&#39;architecture system design avec un Senior Engineering Lead basé en France.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US / Manager Interview (60 min) :&lt;/strong&gt; Échange avec un Director / Partner pour évaluer le fit managérial, opérationnel et la posture client.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rémunération :&lt;/strong&gt; Package :&amp;nbsp; 75 000 € à 85 000 € brut annuel (fixe) + 8 000 € de variable, selon expérience et séniorité.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Présentation de l’entreprise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact est un cabinet de conseil spécialisé en data et en intelligence artificielle, qui accompagne les entreprises pour transformer ces technologies en impact business concret et mesurable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A la croisée du conseil, de la data et de la technologie, nos 2 500 collaborateurs dans 27 pays mettent leurs expertises en commun pour concevoir, développer et déployer des solutions qui répondent aux enjeux de transformation de nos clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Envie d&#39;en savoir plus? Découvrez Artefact, nos expertises et notre culture : &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.artefact.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.artefact.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Chez Artefact, nous sommes convaincus que la diversité des parcours, des expériences et des perspectives fait la richesse de nos équipes. Nous nous engageons à offrir un environnement inclusif et des opportunités équitables, où chacune et chacun peut évoluer et exprimer pleinement son potentiel. Nos recrutements reposent sur les compétences, le potentiel et l&#39;adéquation avec le rôle.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Order Taking squad owns core ordering experiences within SumUp’s Point of Sale app, including the shopping bag, checkout, the catalog experience within ordering, open orders, table management and printer integrations. These capabilities help thousands of hospitality merchants manage orders reliably during daily service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior iOS Engineer, you’ll build new hospitality workflows and evolve established ordering experiences across iOS and Android. You’ll work with SwiftUI on the platform-specific UI and contribute to shared Kotlin Multiplatform business logic. The role involves complex mobile engineering across multi-device synchronisation, shared order state and a large, established application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join a small, experienced and fast-moving squad that works collaboratively through technical refinement, code reviews and pair programming. The team values engineers who communicate directly, challenge assumptions and proactively shape solutions rather than simply execute predefined tasks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build new ordering experiences in SwiftUI, while evolving established capabilities such as table management, kitchen workflows and printer integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to shared Kotlin Multiplatform business logic and help shape the architecture of the ordering domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the reliability and usability of ordering features used daily by hospitality merchants across phones, tablets and POS devices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Android engineers and platform teams to maintain consistent cross-platform behaviour and reliable multi-device order synchronisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in code reviews, pair programming and collaborative testing to maintain a high quality bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help refine and scope upcoming work, bringing technical judgement to product and architectural trade-offs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Mobile Chapter and KMP platform initiatives across the wider POS tribe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience building production iOS applications in Swift, with strong SwiftUI knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a large, established codebase and making pragmatic improvements without requiring a full rewrite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness to learning and contributing to Kotlin and Kotlin Multiplatform; previous hands-on KMP experience is welcome but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently, challenge assumptions, propose solutions proactively and communicate clearly and directly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating closely with Android engineers or other cross-platform partners to align product behaviour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound technical judgement and the ability to balance product delivery, code quality and long-term maintainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 Opportunity to work with a truly global, multicultural team from our Paris location. This involves an office-first setup&lt;br&gt;🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced&lt;br&gt;🚀 Enrolment onto our Virtual Stock Option programme: you will own a stake in SumUp&#39;s future success&lt;br&gt;📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;amp;D budget of €2000 for your individual development, which can be used to attend conferences and/or advance your career through further education&lt;br&gt;💼 Financial security: corporate pension contributions that support your long-term future&lt;br&gt;🏥 Healthcare support: we cover 50% of the monthly cost of your health insurance for your Mutuelle and Prévoyance&lt;br&gt;🚌 Extra allowances: we offer restaurant tickets (Swile) and cover transportation costs&lt;br&gt;🌴 Break4me: 1-month sabbatical after 3 years of service&lt;br&gt;🔗 Referral Bonus: earn additional rewards by referring talented individuals to join the SumUp team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About SumUp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be empowered to do more that matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SumUp, we&#39;re on a mission to empower small businesses across the globe by providing simple and affordable tools that allow them to thrive. Today, over 4 million businesses in 39 markets rely on SumUp as their financial partner to manage payments, finance and customer relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our commitment to small businesses is reflected in&lt;a href=&quot;https://youtu.be/9DG64C3moeQ?si=YpcWuBNBTOQPzeLI&quot;&gt; our diverse team&lt;/a&gt; of over 4,000 SumUppers from over 90 nationalities, united by global collaboration and an innovative mindset.&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.sumup.com/careers/culture/&quot;&gt; Our core values&lt;/a&gt; lay the foundation for who we are and what we stand for, shaping our work culture and driving our success. We foster inclusivity and a continuous learning culture, providing a safe space for personal and professional growth. Our differences make us unique and strong as we strive to create an environment where everyone belongs and feels supported, no matter how they identify.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SumUp is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, actively seeking and embracing diversity in our workforce. We don&#39;t make hiring or employment decisions based on race, colour, religion or religious belief, ethnic or national origin, nationality, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, age or any other basis protected by applicable laws or prohibited by company policy. Our commitment extends beyond recruitment to creating a safe and respectful workplace where harassment of any form is strictly prohibited. Discover more about our culture and opportunities on our&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.sumup.com/careers/&quot;&gt; careers website&lt;/a&gt;, and follow our journey on&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/sumup/&quot;&gt; LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/insidesumup/&quot;&gt; Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.tiktok.com/@insidesumup&quot;&gt; TikTok&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Application Tip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We recognise that candidates feel they need to meet 100% of the job criteria in order to apply for a job. Please note that this is only a guide. If you don’t tick every box, it’s ok too because it means you have room to learn and develop your career at SumUp.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mirakl:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2012, Mirakl has been at the forefront of marketplace innovation, empowering every business to compete in the platform economy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Today, Mirakl’s operating system combines an enterprise marketplace solution (Mirakl Platform) that enables retailers and B2B organizations to launch, scale, and operate marketplaces and dropship, AI-powered multichannel selling (Mirakl Connect), retail media (Mirakl Ads) and an agentic commerce infrastructure (Mirakl Nexus).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With dual headquarters in Boston and Paris, Mirakl helps a global ecosystem of 450+ marketplaces (B2C and B2B) and a network of over 100k third-party marketplace sellers. Brands like Macy’s, Decathlon, Carrefour, Asos, and Airbus Helicopters use Mirakl to grow their businesses in new and remarkable ways.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information: &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.mirakl.com&quot;&gt;www.mirakl.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mirakl in Numbers:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🗓️ Founded in 2012 | Member of French Tech Next40&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;👥 750+ employees in 9 offices worldwide: Paris, Barcelona, Bordeaux, Boston, London, Munich, New York, Sydney, Tokyo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🇫🇷 350+ Mirakl Tech teams members mainly based in France&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⚙️ 5 Saas Solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at Mirakl means accelerating your career alongside ambitious, passionate, and supportive colleagues. We&#39;re proud of the diversity of backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences that make our teams unique.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our 5 values guide how we collaborate:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💡&lt;strong&gt; Work Hard Together:&lt;/strong&gt; Teamwork and collaboration are the foundation of our success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🏆 &lt;strong&gt;Get Things Done: &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We prioritize action and efficiency for impactful results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🚀 &lt;strong&gt;Go Above &amp;amp; Beyond:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; We tackle challenges proactively and always aim for excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🎓 &lt;strong&gt;Succeed Through Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Knowledge sharing and continuous learning are core to our culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🤝 &lt;strong&gt;Satisfy &amp;amp; Empower Clients:&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re committed to our clients&#39; success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team You&#39;ll Join&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join the Product team within Mirakl Platform, working on the Catalog Management pillar.&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll work at the intersection of product, data, and AI: using AI to make our team faster, and helping design the AI agents our customers will use inside Mirakl.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a 6-month internship starting in January/February 2027. You&#39;ll participate in team rituals, gain autonomy quickly, and have the opportunity to present your work regularly to management, offering strong visibility within the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Manager Intern, you&#39;ll play a crucial role in driving data-driven decision-making across the product organization:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Senior Product Manager: Accompany product development end-to-end from discovery and ideation through delivery and go-to-market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and ship AI-automated workflows for PM day-to-day tasks. Examples: automating feedback triage and synthesis, release notes and changelogs, backlog grooming, meeting-to-ticket pipelines, KPI digests, and competitive monitoring. You&#39;ll own these workflows from identifying the pain point to measuring the hours saved.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the design of AI agents embedded in the Mirakl product. Work with the Senior Product Manager, Data Science, and Engineering to define customer-facing agent use cases for operators and sellers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore agentic commerce. Analyze how AI shopping and buying agents change discovery, catalog quality, pricing, and checkout on marketplaces. Map emerging standards and protocols, run small proofs of concept, and help shape product hypotheses and roadmap input&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive data analysis initiatives: Define problems, prepare and preprocess data, conduct statistical analyses, and validate results to support product decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quantify the impact of product releases: Measure and analyze the impact of new features and algorithmic changes through before/after analysis, sizing, hypothesis testing, and segmentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain performance dashboards: Create and maintain dashboards for your pillar and squads to track functional adoption and key performance indicators, including shared dashboards with Customer Success and Sales teams.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring to the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profile &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a gap year internship, end-of-studies internship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical mindset with rigorous problem definition, logical reasoning, and structured thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid foundation in statistics including hypothesis testing, confidence intervals, and methodological choices for before/after impact analysis and group comparisons&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building automated workflows with tools such as n8n, Claude Cowork, or equivalents (Zapier, Make)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python experience is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with a BI tool (Metabase or equivalent) and data visualization best practices is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic knowledge in exploratory data analysis and preprocessing (data cleaning, normalization, outlier management) is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Soft Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious, motivated, and proactive: You take initiative and seek out learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong team collaboration skills: Clear communication skills are essential to work effectively with cross-functional teams including Product, Data Science, Customer Success, and Sales stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast learner with adaptability: You have a strong desire to learn and can quickly adapt to new challenges in a dynamic environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Languages&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Very good level of English required (written and spoken)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monthly stipend range: €1,200 - €1,400&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our Hiring Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We warmly encourage you to apply to this role, even if you think you&#39;re not an exact match.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please click the &quot;Apply&quot; button to submit your application. This helps us make the best possible assessment and get back to you as quickly as possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manual screening of your CV by a recruiter and then an AI-powered screening conversation (10 min) with Emma, Mirakl’s AI Talent Ambassador to explore your background and motivation for the role. You will need to complete this step within 3 days, otherwise we won&#39;t be able to move forward with your application&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TA interview (30-45 minutes) to discuss your experience and answer your questions about Mirakl&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hiring Manager interview (45 minutes) with one of the Product Managers to dive deeper into the role and assess technical fit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;STAR interview (45 minutes) to evaluate alignment with our values and team culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Offer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We welcome collaborators with their diverse perspectives and experiences to power us forward. These often far exceed conventional job requirements and help us create a culture of continuous learning. If you’re ready to join a global leader powering digital transformation for 450+ of the world’s most innovative retailers and B2B organizations.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;As part of our recruitment process, Mirakl processes your personal data to review and manage your application and, where appropriate, to consider your profile for future opportunities. You can exercise your data protection rights at any time, and as further detailed in our policies. For more information about how we process your personal data and your rights, please consult our Recruitment Privacy Notice, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mirakl.com/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; in English and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mirakl.com/fr-FR/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; in French.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We may use Artificial Intelligence (AI) solutions to help streamline our hiring process, including screening applications, analyzing resumes, and assessing responses. While AI helps us work efficiently, all final hiring decisions are made by humans. For more information, visit our &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://info.mirakl.com/ai-guidelines-for-candidates-and-interviews&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;AI Guidelines for Candidates and Interviews&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mirakl:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2012, Mirakl has been at the forefront of marketplace innovation, empowering every business to compete in the platform economy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Today, Mirakl’s operating system combines an enterprise marketplace solution (Mirakl Platform) that enables retailers and B2B organizations to launch, scale, and operate marketplaces and dropship, AI-powered multichannel selling (Mirakl Connect), retail media (Mirakl Ads) and an agentic commerce infrastructure (Mirakl Nexus).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With dual headquarters in Boston and Paris, Mirakl helps a global ecosystem of 450+ marketplaces (B2C and B2B) and a network of over 100k third-party marketplace sellers. Brands like Macy’s, Decathlon, Carrefour, Asos, and Airbus Helicopters use Mirakl to grow their businesses in new and remarkable ways.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information: &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.mirakl.com&quot;&gt;www.mirakl.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mirakl in Numbers:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🗓️ Founded in 2012 | Member of French Tech Next40&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;👥 750+ employees in 9 offices worldwide: Paris, Barcelona, Bordeaux, Boston, London, Munich, New York, Sydney, Tokyo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🇫🇷 350+ Mirakl Tech teams members mainly based in France&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⚙️ 5 Saas Solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at Mirakl means accelerating your career alongside ambitious, passionate, and supportive colleagues. We&#39;re proud of the diversity of backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences that make our teams unique.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our 5 values guide how we collaborate:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💡&lt;strong&gt; Work Hard Together:&lt;/strong&gt; Teamwork and collaboration are the foundation of our success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🏆 &lt;strong&gt;Get Things Done: &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We prioritize action and efficiency for impactful results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🚀 &lt;strong&gt;Go Above &amp;amp; Beyond:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; We tackle challenges proactively and always aim for excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🎓 &lt;strong&gt;Succeed Through Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Knowledge sharing and continuous learning are core to our culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🤝 &lt;strong&gt;Satisfy &amp;amp; Empower Clients:&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re committed to our clients&#39; success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team You&#39;ll Join&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join the Product team of Mirakl Connect, the platform that helps brands and sellers grow their sales across marketplaces and other sales channels. You&#39;ll work closely with the VP Product Connect, the Channel Integration PM and the whole Channel Integration squad.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a 6-month internship starting in January 2027. You&#39;ll participate in team rituals, gain autonomy progressively, and have the opportunity to present your work regularly to management, offering strong visibility within the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Your Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Choosing and building the right channels is one of our biggest growth levers. As a Product Manager Intern, your mission will be to help the team prepare and assess new channel opportunities, reduce uncertainty before development starts and contribute to successful integrations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your work will help the squad bring together the key information, questions, risks and opportunities before development begins.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Concretely, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help pre-qualify channels:&lt;/strong&gt; Map the marketplace landscape by country and vertical, and contribute to a first-level assessment of each channel: technical integration effort, functional coverage with Mirakl Connect, and business potential (seller demand).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Explore channel requirements: &lt;/strong&gt;Review channel API specifications and requirements across catalog, offers, orders and logistics, and test them hands-on (e.g. with Postman). With support from the team, identify key questions, dependencies, risks and areas that require further investigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prepare build-ready inputs:&lt;/strong&gt; Turn your analyses into useful inputs for the squad, such as data mappings, process diagrams, edge cases, open questions for channel partners and first drafts of user stories.&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Talk to the field:&lt;/strong&gt; Interview sellers, Sales and Customer Success teams, and channel partner teams to turn scattered feedback into clear insights and product recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to channel builds: &lt;/strong&gt;Alongside the Channel Integration PM and the squad, help refine specifications and user stories, contribute to backlog discussions, answer functional questions and participate in QA and go-live preparation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build AI-powered tools to scale channel work:&lt;/strong&gt; Use AI tools to accelerate research, analysis and prototyping. For example, you may help create an agent that analyzes channel documentation, a Q&amp;amp;A assistant for Sales and Customer Success or AI-assisted prototypes to explore mappings and integration flows.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;After 3 months: A broad set of channels pre-analyzed at a high level, with a first assessment of technical integration effort and functional coverage, contributing to channel pre-qualification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;After 6 months: Several channels analyzed in depth and handed over to the squad as build-ready, an active contribution to channel builds, and at least one AI tool in daily use by the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring to the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profile &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a gap year internship or end-of-studies internship (engineering school, business school or university)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in e-commerce, marketplaces and retail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A structured mindset, with the ability to turn a broad or ambiguous question into a clear and actionable analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine curiosity for understanding how products, processes and systems work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in a start-up or scale up, in e-commerce, consulting, business analysis or project work is a plus, but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Technical Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on with APIs:&lt;/strong&gt; You understand what an API is and how systems exchange data, and you can read API documentation and make simple API calls (e.g. with Postman). Familiarity with data formats (JSON, XML) or integration concepts is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data and spreadsheet skills:&lt;/strong&gt; You are comfortable using spreadsheets to analyze, compare and synthesize information. Experience with dashboards or SQL would be a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on with AI tools:&lt;/strong&gt; You use AI tools daily and critically to improve research, analysis and product work. Experience creating prompts, automations or agents is a plus.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Soft Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curious, proactive and rigorous: &lt;/strong&gt;You take initiative, ask thoughtful questions and dig until the key unknowns are clarified.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong communication and collaboration skills:&lt;/strong&gt; You communicate clearly with different stakeholders, collaborate effectively in cross-functional environments and can summarize complex information into clear, actionable conclusions for different audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fast learner with adaptability:&lt;/strong&gt; You pick up new domains quickly and are comfortable learning unfamiliar concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Critical thinker:&lt;/strong&gt; You can challenge assumptions, assess the quality of information and distinguish facts from hypotheses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Languages&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English is mandatory, both written and spoken, as it is our working language with the team and channel partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Another European language is a plus.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monthly stipend range: €1,200 - €1,400&lt;/p&gt;
